# The committed pictures live here: golden/parity/screens/<volume>/<step>.png,
# one per screenshot step of the extended tour (SCHEMA.md §2.1.3).
#
# THE PICTURES ARE HERE, AND NOTHING IS IGNORED. The capture wave of §6.1 took
# them from the finished build and committed them in the same commit as the
# baselines that name them, because a baseline naming a picture that is not
# there is a broken gate. `compare.mjs` compares every picture it has a twin
# for, perceptually, at the threshold in `pixels.mjs`.
#
# THIS FILE STAYS, EMPTY OF RULES, ON PURPOSE. The line it used to carry --
# `*.png` -- was the switch that kept an unfinished build from being golden,
# and deleting it was the last act of the wave. A picture that landed here
# without being committed would be a gate that says nothing, so the absence of
# a rule is written down rather than left to be inferred from an absent file.
#
# A walk's picture with no committed twin is still reported as *not captured*,
# which is not a pass: a new screenshot step arrives red until somebody takes
# its picture, which is the way round this directory wants to be wrong.
